  "notes": [
   "The page image is a low-resolution overview of the whole booklet (steps 1-10); I recorded only the pieces I could identify with reasonable confidence.",
   "Step 1: 6157 wheel-holder plate under the end of the two black 1x8 plates; step 2 adds two grey 2x4 plates and the black 2x2 wheel-holder plate (4600) on the underside.",
   "Step 5 looks identical to step 4 at this resolution, so nothing was added for it.",
   "Steps 6-10: bracket positions (step 7), wheel on the pin (step 8), curved brick (step 9) and 1x4 stud plate (step 10) are approximate. The black wedge plates, slopes, tiles, flags and tyres visible in the pictures could not be resolved and are omitted.",
   "Ids b1-b16 used; the next page should continue from b17.",
   "Page 2 is low resolution, so the identification of the black pieces in step 11 is a best guess: one 3x1 slope on top and two 1x2 slopes.",
   "Step 12: the orange stripe is read as the pearl gold grille tile, and the clear brown piece as a trans-brown cheese slope.",
   "Steps 13-14: the large balloon tyres on 11x12 wheels are assumed to go on the 2x2 wheel-holder plate b1. The small 14x9 tyres on 8x9 wheels are assumed to go on b6. Which wheel goes on which holder could not be confirmed.",
   "Step 15 inset (a black wedge plate with a small plate pair, built mirrored left and right) is not recorded, because the pieces could not be identified. The remaining parts list items (43722, 43723, 44676, 2540, 3794b, black 54200, 3068b, 6141 x3, and others) are therefore not all placed.",
   "Ids b17-b29 used; the model is complete after step 15.",
   "Added the pieces from the parts list that earlier pages had not placed: 2 black 3460, 1 grey 3020, 2 grey 3700, the 2654 round plate, a tan 3710, 4 black 3023, 3068b, 2 x 3794b, wedge plates 43722 and 43723, 2 x 2540, 2 x 44676 flags, 2 black and 1 trans-brown 54200, 3 x 6141 and 2 x 85984.",
   "The booklet images are too small to show exactly where these pieces go in steps 11-15, so their rests_on links are best guesses. Positions are plausible, not verified.",
   "The checker's list showed some types as fully missing even though I had placed them earlier (for example 2412b, 4286, 30028, 42610, 3700). I did not re-add those, to avoid duplicates. Earlier placements stay: b20 (2412b), b17 (4286), b28/b29 (30028), b14 (42610), b8 (3700).",
   "Together with b1-b29 this gives all 57 pieces in the parts list. The step 15 insets show the left/right mirrored wedge plate with a small plate pair. These are represented by b44/b45 with b42/b43 and b46/b47.",
   "No new pieces added. The 'missing' list is the same as in the last check, although the previous correction placed those parts, so I think the check is not counting the pieces I already returned. Adding them again would create duplicates and push the totals over the parts list.",
   "My records, b1-b57, match the parts list at 57 pieces: 2412b b20; 2540 b46,b47; 2654 b35; 30028 b28,b29; 3020 b4,b5,b32; 3023 tan b9 and black b37-b40; 3068b b41; 3460 b2,b3,b30,b31; 3700 b8,b33,b34; 3710 b11,b36; 3794b b42,b43; 42610 b14; 4286 b17; 43722 b44; 43723 b45.",
   "Same records, rest of the list: 44676 b48,b49; 44728 b12,b13; 4600 b6; 54200 black b50,b51 and trans-brown b21,b52; 56890 b24,b25; 6014b b22,b23; 6141 b7,b53-b55; 6157 b1; 6232 b10; 74967 b26,b27; 85984 b18,b19,b56,b57; 92593 b16; 93273 b15.",
   "Positions and rests_on links for b30-b57 are best guesses because the booklet images are low resolution. If the checker still reports these types as missing, the pieces from the earlier correction may not have been merged, and that would need checking on your side."
  ]
